# 📊 Netflix Data Cleaning and Visualization Project

This project involves cleaning and visualizing Netflix content data using **PostgreSQL** and **Tableau**. The goal is to demonstrate practical skills in data wrangling, transformation, and dashboard design.

---

## 🗂️ Dataset Overview

The dataset includes Netflix titles added from **2008 to 2021**, with the oldest content dating back to **1925**. The cleaned version of the dataset was used for visualizations.

- ✅ Source: [Original dataset](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/shivamb/netflix-shows)
- 📁 Cleaned Dataset: `netflix1_cleaned.csv`

---

## 🧼 Data Cleaning (PostgreSQL)

The cleaning process focused on:
- **Removing nulls**
- **Populating missing values**
- **Splitting and dropping unnecessary columns**
- **Ensuring consistency for Tableau visualization**

### ✅ Null Handling Summary

| Column        | Nulls Found | Action Taken |
|---------------|-------------|--------------|
| `director`    | ~2634       | Filled using relationship with `movie_cast`; remaining set as `"Not Given"` |
| `country`     | ~831        | Filled using `director`; remaining set as `"Not Given"` |
| `date_added`  | 10          | Rows deleted |
| `rating`      | 4           | Rows deleted |
| `duration`    | 3           | Rows deleted |
| `movie_cast`  | ~825        | Column dropped (not relevant for analysis) |
| `description` | -           | Dropped (not used in visualization) |

### 🧹 Other Cleaning Steps

- **Duplicates**: Verified using `show_id` – none found
- **Split multiple countries** in the `country` column and retained only the **first** for mapping
- **Dropped** unnecessary columns: `movie_cast`, `description`
- **Final columns** used in visualization:
  - `show_id`, `type`, `title`, `director`, `country`, `date_added`, `release_year`, `rating`, `duration`, `listed_in`

---

## 📈 Visualization (Tableau)

An interactive dashboard was created using Tableau to explore insights such as:
- Distribution of content by country
- Content trends over the years
- Most common ratings and genres
- Director-based content analysis

